1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
How do you TURN something?

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,200
sin and cos do the whole job.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
One arrow. Across 3, up 4 — that is all an arrow is.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:09,600
Now turn it. Where does it end up?

5
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:12,000
From last time: cos θ = 0.8, sin θ = 0.6.

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,800
Across is cos, up is sin. Four slots filled, for free.

7
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,000
The 3 goes into x. The 4 goes into y.

8
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,800
The equation is full. Read it out.

9
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,600
new x = 3(0.8) − 4(0.6). That is 2.4 − 2.4.

10
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,000
The same number, twice. It cancels. new x = 0.

11
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
THAT is what the minus is for.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,400
new y = 1.8 + 3.2 = 5. Across 0, up 5 — dead straight up.

13
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,800
5 long before. 5 long after. Turning never stretches.

14
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
We learned this at school.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Nobody ever said what for.

16
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Send this to your school friend — and tell them THIS is how it's solved.

17
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Follow for the math behind AI. @observer.collapse
